# Testing Development Guide

## Testing Principles

- **Unit Tests**: Test behavior, not implementation. Keep tests small, isolated, and mock external dependencies. Test error/edge cases.
- **Integration Tests**: Test realistic user scenarios with minimal mocking. Verify API contracts and database interactions.
- **E2E Tests**: Focus on critical user paths. Use data attributes for selectors. Implement proper waits. Keep tests independent.

## Quick Commands

### Unit & Integration Tests

```bash
# Run all unit tests (primary command)
npm run test:unit

# Run unit tests in watch mode
npm run test:unit:watch

# Run unit tests with coverage
npm run test:unit:coverage

# Comprehensive test suite (unit + E2E)
npm test

# CI test suite
npm run test:ci
```

### End-to-End Tests

```bash
# Run all E2E tests (most comprehensive)
npm run test:e2e

# Specific test categories
npm run test:e2e:auth-only          # Authentication tests only
npm run test:e2e:public-only        # Unauthenticated tests only  
npm run test:e2e:authenticated-only # Protected route tests only

# Debugging E2E tests
npm run test:e2e:debug              # Step-through debugging
npm run test:e2e:headed             # Visible browser mode
npm run test:e2e:update-snapshots   # Update visual snapshots
npm run test:e2e:report             # View HTML test report
```

### Code Coverage

